      {
        "chunk_id": "e8d023727367b0f20a7c3b6060eee5e1",
        "text": "5.1.1. Using Lists as Stacks\n\nThe list methods make it very easy to use a list as a stack, where the last element added is the first element retrieved (“last-in, first-out”). To add an item to the top of the stack, use append(). To retrieve an item from the top of the stack, use pop() without an explicit index. For example:",
